  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "A function assigns exactly one output to each input. The EST I tests function notation, composition, inverses, and transformations.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Functions",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Notation: \\( f(x) \\) means the output of \\( f \\) at input \\( x \\). Composition: \\( (f\\circ g)(x)=f(g(x)) \\). Inverse: \\( f^{-1} \\) reverses \\( f \\); find it by swapping \\( x \\) and \\( y \\) and solving for \\( y \\). Transformation: \\( f(x)+k \\) shifts up, \\( f(x-h) \\) shifts right, \\( -f(x) \\) reflects over \\( x \\)-axis.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Composition",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (f\\circ g)(x)=f(g(x)) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Inverse",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "swap \\( x,y \\) then solve",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Shift up k",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f(x)+k \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Shift right h",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f(x-h) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 3.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "If \\( f(x)=2x+1 \\) and \\( g(x)=x^2 \\), find \\( f(g(3)) \\). \\[ g(3)=9,\\quad f(9)=2(9)+1=19. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "<h3>Domain and range</h3>The <strong>domain</strong> is all valid inputs; the <strong>range</strong> is all possible outputs. For \\( f(x)=\\sqrt{x-3} \\), the domain is \\( x\\geq 3 \\) (argument under the root must be non-negative). For \\( f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{x-2} \\), exclude \\( x=2 \\) from the domain.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Inverse function",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Find \\(f^{-1}(x)\\) for \\(f(x) = \\dfrac{3x-1}{2}\\). <p>Let \\(y = \\dfrac{3x-1}{2}\\). Swap \\(x\\) and \\(y\\): \\(x = \\dfrac{3y-1}{2} \\Rightarrow 2x+1 = 3y \\Rightarrow y = \\dfrac{2x+1}{3}\\).</p><p>So \\(f^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{2x+1}{3}\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "The graph of \\(y = f(x)\\) is shifted 3 units right and reflected in the \\(x\\)-axis. Write the new equation in terms of \\(f\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(y = -f(x-3)\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
